      "text": "To find the value of \\(8a - 4b + 2c - d\\), we first need to determine the coefficients \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) of the polynomial \\(f(x) = ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\).\n\nFrom the graph, we observe that the polynomial has roots at \\(x = 0\\), \\(x = 1\\), and \\(x = 2\\). This indicates that the polynomial can be factored as:\n\\[ f(x) = x(x-1)(x-2) \\]\n\nWe expand this product to find the coefficients:\n\\[ f(x) = x(x-1)(x-2) \\]\n\nFirst, expand \\((x-1)(x-2)\\):\n\\[ (x-1)(x-2) = x^2 - 2x - x + 2 = x^2 - 3x + 2 \\]\n\nThen, multiply the result by \\(x\\):\n\\[ f(x) = x(x^2 - 3x + 2) = x^3 - 3x^2 + 2x \\]\n\nComparing this with \\(f(x) = ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\), we identify the coefficients:\n\\[ a = 1, \\quad b = -3, \\quad c = 2, \\quad d = 0 \\]\n\nNow, we calculate \\(8a - 4b + 2c - d\\):\n\\[ 8a - 4b + 2c - d = 8(1) - 4(-3) + 2(2) - 0 \\]\n\nCompute each term:\n\\[ 8a = 8 \\]\n\\[ 4b = 4(-3) = -12 \\]\n\\[ 2c = 2(2) = 4 \\]\n\nSubstitute these values back into the expression:\n\\[ 8a - 4b + 2c - d = 8 - 12 + 4 + 0 \\]\n\nCombine the terms:\n\\[ 8 - 12 + 4 = 0 \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(8a - 4b + 2c - d\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{0}\n\\]",
